<section class="section" id="guidance">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Guidance System</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">How to Actually Follow This Roadmap</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle">A roadmap without a system is a wish list. These habits determine whether this journey produces genuine expertise.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="guidance-grid">

      <div class="guidance-card">
        <div class="guidance-card-body">
          <div class="guidance-icon-row">
            <span class="guidance-icon-glyph">📅</span>
            <div class="guidance-card-title">The Weekly Operating Rhythm</div>
          </div>
          <p class="guidance-card-desc">Split every week: <strong>60%</strong> course content, <strong>30%</strong> implementation from scratch, <strong>10%</strong> writing (the Feynman test). Without this split, all time goes to passive watching.</p>
          <div class="guidance-tip">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12"/></svg>
            Passive video watching gives a false sense of progress. The 30% implementation slot is non-negotiable.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="guidance-card">
        <div class="guidance-card-body">
          <div class="guidance-icon-row">
            <span class="guidance-icon-glyph">🏗️</span>
            <div class="guidance-card-title">The Project Ladder</div>
          </div>
          <p class="guidance-card-desc">One major deliverable per stage. After Stage 4: train your own GPT. After Stage 7: deploy a live ML API. Treat your GitHub as your technical resume — employers care about what you built.</p>
          <div class="guidance-tip">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12"/></svg>
            A live, publicly accessible ML demo is the single most impactful portfolio item you can have.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="guidance-card">
        <div class="guidance-card-body">
          <div class="guidance-icon-row">
            <span class="guidance-icon-glyph">📝</span>
            <div class="guidance-card-title">Knowledge Consolidation</div>
          </div>
          <p class="guidance-card-desc">Set up an Obsidian or Notion vault. For every concept: intuition, math, code, failure modes. Publish blog posts to force clarity of thought. ML involves thousands of disconnected concepts.</p>
          <div class="guidance-tip">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12"/></svg>
            If you can't explain it simply, you don't understand it yet.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="guidance-card">
        <div class="guidance-card-body">
          <div class="guidance-icon-row">
            <span class="guidance-icon-glyph">📄</span>
            <div class="guidance-card-title">The Paper-Reading Habit</div>
          </div>
          <p class="guidance-card-desc">One classic paper per week from Stage 4 onwards. Strategy: abstract/conclusion → intro → skim results → read methods. Never read linearly on the first pass.</p>
          <div class="guidance-tip">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12"/></svg>
            The field moves faster than textbooks. Expert = comfortable reading raw research.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="guidance-card">
        <div class="guidance-card-body">
          <div class="guidance-icon-row">
            <span class="guidance-icon-glyph">⚠️</span>
            <div class="guidance-card-title">Avoid Tutorial Hell</div>
          </div>
          <p class="guidance-card-desc">Do not collect courses — finish them. Do not treat <code>model.fit()</code> as magic. True learning only happens when you're stuck debugging your own code, not following along with a video.</p>
          <div class="guidance-tip">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12"/></svg>
            Tutorial-following gives false competence. Build from scratch whenever possible.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="guidance-card guidance-card--cta">
        <div class="guidance-card-body">
          <div class="guidance-icon-row">
            <span class="guidance-icon-glyph">🧭</span>
            <div class="guidance-card-title">Full Guidance on Dashboard</div>
          </div>
          <p class="guidance-card-desc">The interactive dashboard includes a complete Guidance section with full details, plus a "Stay Updated" section for curated newsletters, blogs, and paper discovery tools.</p>
          <div class="guidance-tip">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12"/></svg>
            Navigate to Guidance → in the sidebar of the dashboard to access all five habit systems.
          </div>
          <a href="/dashboard" class="guidance-cta-btn">
            Open Dashboard
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
